  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_nail_cb19ca68acec5ec001f2517cafcc98219b3edde2feeeddd9f6472dc564178d772a4">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>nail (see also clavus) | nail (cf. clavus) | nail | nails 481, 484 (see also clavus) | nail for making brigandines, body-armor for foot-soldiers made of iron rings or small thin iron plates sewn onto canvas, linen or leather and covered with a similar material. Originally in pairs (front and back), ergo often in the plural (OED s.v. brigandine) | 25, | arming-nail, forming part of armor (OED arming vgl. n. 1b) | nail for making brigandyns | middle quality nails</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
